    "_size_classes": "estimate (UK roundabout practice, DMRB CD 116 style values recalled, not checked): by ring centreline radius. Entry fillets are tight (slow entries), exit fillets generous (easy exits); small rings get an over-run apron. splitter_length_m / splitter_width_m are the KERBED island: a short teardrop (roughly a triangle with a rounded nose) widest at the ring edge. Measured from the private reference photos (aerial 09 M181 and 41 Kolbaskowo, street 28, GSV Brynich and Thetford Rd): about 15-25 m long and 4-6 m wide at the base for a 2-lane approach, a length to width ratio of 3:1 to 5:1; any longer taper is painted ladder hatching, not kerb. Surface (reference photos: GSV Thetford Rd and Brynich show dark tarmac inside a pale kerb, street 28 a grassed 25 x 6 m island on a 20 mph street, aerial 09 grass on the large rural ring; Kolbaskowo, Poland, shows paving blocks, which is not the UK default): asphalt for the small and mid classes, grass for the largest class. The length is scaled by splitter_speed_factors (about 17 m at 30 mph, 26 m at 40-50 mph, 40 m at 60 mph on a ring of 25-50 m radius).",
